finding: Blocking: src/cli/publish-itch.ts:135-138 invokes butler status with spawnSync and no timeout; src/cli/publish.ts:418 calls it before checking the processing deadline at :424. A stuck status process therefore blocks the event loop indefinitely and never reaches the advertised ten-minute refusal. Reproduced with a local substitute butler that execs sleep: runButler remained blocked until an outer process timeout killed the caller. The recorded-response tests only exercise returned answers, so they do not hold this failure mode. Bound non-interactive status invocations (including the initial setup probe), and make the polling deadline effective across child execution, with a local hanging-child regression test. No real itch.io hang is asserted; the missing bound is in Shallot's wait.
